  "scope": "Nonlinear update admissibility/conservation; conservative-to-primitive derivative connection; frozen and spatially varying principal-update energy estimates; grid-independent 3D embedding; exact noncontraction witness; actual entropy derivatives, convexity, finite averaging bound and local Euler entropy balance. The variable-coefficient estimate assumes explicit state and spatial-difference bounds. Existence, nonlinear full-solve stability, continuum solver accuracy and matching work optimality remain unproved. Actual nonlinear finite-step entropy dissipation is checked under explicit convex-region, curvature, flux, viscosity and timestep conditions. Uniform trajectory membership and those conditions for the current numerical settings remain unproved. Concrete physical-region bounds and initial-family membership are checked. A checked obstruction shows that the global sufficient viscosity criterion cannot certify the current wave-speed recipe on that region, even with improved valid curvature constants. It does not refute actual solver stability. An alternative existing logarithmic-mean entropy-conservative flux plus LF diffusion has a checked exact entropy identity, physical-flux consistency and nonpositive face residual for any nonnegative diffusion. With positive coefficients, a finite real-arithmetic halving search finds a positive, admissible, conservative step satisfying a finite-step entropy decrease condition. The zero-dissipation case is also proved stationary. There is no uniform retry bound, certified floating-point guard, proof of reaching the target time, continuum error bound or total-work optimality result."
}
